  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements is not a tautology?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5evb8",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rEdeB",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>∨</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Id5k3",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6rIEA",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∧</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is subset of <math><mi>r</mi></math>, so&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a subset of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Hence,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology.<br />Similarly,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology because <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a subset of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Similarly,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a subset of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Hence,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi></math> is false if <math><mi>p</mi></math> is true, <math><mi>q</mi></math> is true and <math><mi>r</mi></math> is false. Hence,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi></math> is not a tautology",
